# Decision Workflow

Purpose:
  Lifecycle of a decision from proposal to verification.

States:
  proposed:
    Next: review|rejected
    Who: AI or Human

  review:
    Next: approved|rejected|revised
    Who: Human or Agent
    Gate: human approval required for architectural/security/business

  approved:
    Next: implemented
    Who: Human
    Gate: approval recorded

  rejected:
    Next: archived
    Who: Human
    Gate: feedback recorded

  revised:
    Next: review
    Who: AI
    Gate: revision feedback incorporated

  implemented:
    Next: verified
    Who: AI or Human
    Gate: tasks completed

  verified:
    Next: closed
    Who: Human or QA
    Gate: verification criteria met

  superseded:
    Next: archived
    Who: Human
    Gate: new decision approved

  archived:
    Final state

Flow:
  proposed -> review -> approved -> implemented -> verified -> closed
                   -> rejected -> archived
                   -> revised -> review
                   -> superseded -> archived

Rules:
  [DW1] Every significant change MUST have a decision record.
  [DW2] Architectural decisions MUST be human-approved.
  [DW3] Security decisions MUST be human-approved.
  [DW4] AI MAY propose technical decisions.
  [DW5] Human MAY override AI decisions.
  [DW6] Superseded decisions MUST reference new decision.
  [DW7] Conflicting decisions MUST be resolved before implementation.
  [DW8] Decision rationale MUST be recorded.
  [DW9] Implementation MUST reference decision ID.
  [DW10] Verification MUST reference decision criteria.

State: +
